  "event_preview": "Virginia International Raceway is a 3.27-mile (5.263 km), 17-turn permanent road course in Alton, Virginia, an old-school roller-coaster layout on the Virginia-North Carolina border defined by the Climbing Esses, the Oak Tree and a long back straight. The Michelin GT Challenge at VIR was the ninth round of the 2026 IMSA WeatherTech SportsCar Championship and the only all-GT weekend of the season, scheduled for 2 hours and 40 minutes on Sunday, August 23, with GTP and LMP2 absent. Twenty-three cars were entered: 10 in GTD Pro and 13 in GTD, including a one-off GTD Pro Aston Martin for Car Blanche with Valentin Hasse-Clot and Marco Sorensen.\n\nConnor De Phillippi and Neil Verhagen led GTD Pro in the No. 1 Paul Miller Racing BMW, 15 points clear of Tommy Milner and Nicky Catsburg in the No. 4 Corvette, with Harry King and Nick Tandy a further six points back in the No. 77 AO Racing Porsche. Christopher Mies and Frederic Vervisch sat 99 points off the lead in the No. 65 Ford; two-time 2026 winners Ben Barnicoat and Jack Hawksworth were 113 back in the No. 14 Vasser Sullivan Lexus. The No. 3 Corvette of Antonio Garcia and Alexander Sims arrived as the defending overall VIR winners, Garcia chasing a series-leading fifth victory at the track. In GTD, Eduardo Barrichello's No. 27 Heart of Racing Aston Martin led the standings; Philip Ellis and Russell Ward sat 24 points behind after consecutive wins at Canadian Tire Motorsport Park and Road America, Robby Foley and Patrick Gallagher were 26 back in the No. 96 Turner BMW, and Aaron Telitz and Benjamin Pedersen 45 back in the No. 12 Lexus.\n\nIMSA WeatherTech Championship qualifying records at Virginia International Raceway belong to Madison Snow in GTD Pro (1:43.206, 2024) and Ross Gunn in GTD (1:43.356, 2021).",
  "event_preview_ru": "Virginia International Raceway — постоянная 17-поворотная трасса длиной 3,27 мили (5,263 км) в Alton, Virginia, старая «американские горки» на границе Virginia и North Carolina: Climbing Esses, Oak Tree и длинная задняя прямая. Michelin GT Challenge at VIR стал девятым этапом IMSA WeatherTech SportsCar Championship 2026 и единственным полностью GT-уик-эндом сезона, планировался на 2 часа 40 минут в воскресенье, 23 августа, без GTP и LMP2. Заявлены 23 машины: 10 в GTD Pro и 13 в GTD, включая разовую заявку Car Blanche в GTD Pro на Aston Martin с Valentin Hasse-Clot и Marco Sorensen.\n\nConnor De Phillippi и Neil Verhagen лидировали в GTD Pro на BMW No. 1 Paul Miller Racing, на 15 очков впереди Tommy Milner и Nicky Catsburg на Corvette No. 4; Harry King и Nick Tandy на Porsche No. 77 AO Racing отставали ещё на шесть. Christopher Mies и Frederic Vervisch на Ford No. 65 были в 99 очках от лидера; двукратные победители 2026 года Ben Barnicoat и Jack Hawksworth на Lexus No. 14 Vasser Sullivan — в 113. Corvette No. 3 Antonio Garcia и Alexander Sims приехали как действующие победители VIR в абсолюте; Garcia претендовал на пятую победу серии на этой трассе. В GTD лидировал Aston Martin No. 27 Heart of Racing Eduardo Barrichello; Philip Ellis и Russell Ward отставали на 24 очка после побед подряд на Canadian Tire Motorsport Park и Road America, Robby Foley и Patrick Gallagher на BMW No. 96 Turner — на 26, Aaron Telitz и Benjamin Pedersen на Lexus No. 12 — на 45.\n\nКвалификационные рекорды IMSA WeatherTech Championship на Virginia International Raceway: GTD Pro — Madison Snow (1:43.206, 2024), GTD — Ross Gunn (1:43.356, 2021).",
